{
  "_comment": "Which permission each KH route needs, read by app/auth.py. A method of * matches any method; {name:path} matches the rest of the path. /v1 routes (stage F) check namespace roles in app/caps. kinds: public (no sign-in), authenticated (any registered person; the route filters what it returns), ns (a /v1/{ns} route: a service token only for its own namespace, a person checked by the route), project (permission on the project the request touches), kh (a KH-wide permission), maintainer. project_from lists where the project id is read from, first hit wins; default_project applies when none is given - requests without a project touch the orchestrator, which members may read but not change. A route missing here is open to maintainers only. \"worker\": true (roadmap E-5, app/caps/people.py) additionally lets the kh_people worker token (role distiller) call that route while KH_CAP_PEOPLE=on and KH_DISTILL_WORKER is dry or on; without that module the rule is exactly its kind. \"agents\": true (roadmap E-5 phase 5, app/caps/improve.py) additionally lets the kh_people worker token and active agent principals of the namespaces in kh_people settings.improve.agent_namespaces (default kh_ops, ops_pilot) call that route while KH_CAP_IMPROVE=on; without that module the rule is exactly its kind.",
